{"condition": "9_engine_v2_full", "prompt_id": "t_ng_07", "category": "negative_constraints", "instruction": "Name three animals that live in Africa without mentioning lions or elephants.", "response": "There are many other fascinating creatures that inhabit the diverse landscapes of Africa. Here are three examples:\n\n1. **Cheetahs**: Known for their incredible speed and agility, cheetahs are the fastest land animals on Earth. They can reach speeds of up to 70 miles per hour (113 kilometers per hour) when chasing prey.\n\n2. **Giraffes**: These gentle giants are easily recognizable by their long necks and spots. They are native to sub-Saharan Africa and are herbivores, feeding primarily on leaves from acacia trees.\n\n3. **Okapis**: Okapis are unique-looking primates found only in the dense forests of the Democratic Republic of Congo. They have a distinctive appearance with reddish-brown fur, a distinctive blue tongue, and", "raw_text": " There are many other fascinating creatures that inhabit the diverse landscapes of Africa. Here are three examples:\n\n1. **Cheetahs**: Known for their incredible speed and agility, cheetahs are the fastest land animals on Earth. They can reach speeds of up to 70 miles per hour (113 kilometers per hour) when chasing prey.\n\n2. **Giraffes**: These gentle giants are easily recognizable by their long necks and spots. They are native to sub-Saharan Africa and are herbivores, feeding primarily on leaves from acacia trees.\n\n3. **Okapis**: Okapis are unique-looking primates found only in the dense forests of the Democratic Republic of Congo. They have a distinctive appearance with reddish-brown fur, a distinctive blue tongue, and", "n_new_tokens": 160, "stop_reason": "max_tokens", "stop_string": null, "prompt_tokens": 17, "latency_s": 6.48116770805791, "ms_per_token": 40.50729817536194, "stop_events": [{"t": 14, "score": 0.4025}, {"t": 19, "score": 0.2952}, {"t": 21, "score": 0.0004}, {"t": 47, "score": 0.3374}, {"t": 72, "score": 0.35